Velodrome Splice
Ingredients: SKATE PUNK & POP PUNK + EUPHORIC, ENERGETIC & JOLLY + Accordion
Creative Catalyst: It descends from carnival musicians who perform only during solar eclipses.

Velodrome Splice sounds like a massive, sun-blasted outdoor halfpipe built directly on top of a migrating circus fairground. Blisteringly fast, palm-muted power chord progressions and hyper-kinetic, four-on-the-floor pop-punk drum beats smash headfirst into dizzying, full-throttle polka rhythms. The sonic core is anchored by an overdriven, air-starved diatonic accordion pumped so aggressively through a vintage guitar cabinet that it squeals like a distorted fuzz-pedal, riding side-by-side with gleaming vocal harmonies and soaring, triumphant brass-synth leads that radiate pure, reckless joy.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 188-202 BPM; an unrelenting, galloping ska-punk beat driven by hyper-fast hi-hats and a relentless, bouncing two-step polka bassline.
- Harmonic Palette: Major-heavy modal scales (mostly G and C major) dripping with sugary, anthemic pop-punk hooks offset by minor-key accordion waltzes.
- Production Signatures: Battered cassette-saturated room mics on the drums to capture live skatepark acoustics, an overdriven accordion compressed to sound like a searing lead guitar, and ultra-wide, multi-tracked gang vocals shouting euphoric counter-melodies.
- Dynamics: Explosive wall-of-sound choruses that burst open from stripped-down, hand-clapping acoustic verses, culminating in chaotic, double-time polka breakdowns where the accordion and distorted guitars trade blistering solos.

Scene & Origin Lore
Born in the dusty municipal skateparks of regional coastal towns just as the midday sun began to crescent into shadow, Velodrome Splice was forged by grease-painted teenagers who spent their summers tearing up concrete bowls and their winters running away with the traveling flat-pack carnival. Adorned in neon safety gear, frayed flannel vests stitched with yellow velvet ribbons, and heavy-duty knee pads scuffed with greasepaint, this hyper-active subculture treats every session like a fleeting celestial holiday. They skate through the fading light of accidental eclipses while pumping breathless, joyful punk anthems out of wheel-mounted PA systems, keeping time with the ancestral pulse of shadow-chasers.

